# Round XXIX Track C — AFTER fixture for `E_EnumerateOnNonIterator`. The
# fix-it advice from `_before.gg`'s diagnostic tells the user to write
# `.iter().enumerate()`; this fixture applies that advice and asserts the
# result actually compiles + runs. Guarded by
# `tests/lints.rs::advice_fixtures_have_working_remedy`.
int main():
    Set[int] s = {}
    s.add(7)
    s.add(8)
    for (i, x) in s.iter().enumerate():
        print(f"{i}->{x}")
    return 0
